Custody provides controls (data-aware policy, approval gates, a
tamper-evident audit log, and isolated execution) that can support
HIPAA-aligned programs. It is not a HIPAA certification, does not
ensure compliance on its own, and does not replace a business
associate agreement, a risk assessment, or an institution's own
review process. See README.md ("What Custody is not") and
docs/threat-model.md before relying on it for a specific workflow.
